{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he went to the land because of Jacob his brother.</b> Its sense is: 'and he went to the land of Seir,' for there was his place, in the manner written above: ״וישב ביום ההוא עשו לדרכו שעירה״ — and that day Esau set out on his way to Seir; and so it is written (Genesis 36): ״וישב עשו בהר שעיר״ — and Esau settled in Mount Seir. And R. Abraham z\"l wrote: this Mount Seir is near the land of Canaan, as it is said (Deuteronomy 2:8): ״ונעבור מאת אחינו בני עשו היושבים בשעיר״. And it is written (Deuteronomy 1:2): ״אחד עשר יום מחורב דרך הר שעיר״ — eleven days from Horeb by the way of Mount Seir; and it is not the Mount Seir of the land where the children of Edom dwell now, for that land is none other than the land of Javan."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:56.816343463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}